    <ReasonableCauseExplanation documentId="R000004" softwareId="24021167" softwareVersionNum="v1.00">
      <ExplanationTxt>We filed a form to change our tax year. We got approval for form and were instructed to complete short year tax form. When we went to go file our normal 990-N we could not file online. Our initial call to the IRS told us it was okay to miss this filing because we would not be penalized unless we did not submit 3 years of returns. Later, we received other mail notices because of the end of year change that created lots of confusion. After many back and forth phone calls with the IRS, who was extremely helpful most recently, we were able to figure out what the issue was and were instructed to submit this form. I was told by the representative that these notes are on our file. Thank you so much for your help!</ExplanationTxt>
    </ReasonableCauseExplanation>
